        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Ice-cream sales and reported crime can both rise during hot weather. That does not mean buying ice cream causes crime. Temperature changes behavior in ways that can affect both measurements. This third-variable problem is one reason an observed relationship cannot establish a causal direction on its own."
        },
